course: dictionary
lesson: 11033
title: Weaken: losing strength, or giving in
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To weaken means to become less strong, or to make someone or something less strong. It can also mean to start to give in or change your mind. The opposite of weaken is strengthen.
explain: «Astronauts' muscles and bones weaken in space, so they exercise about two hours every day.» The clue is the exercise: they work hard to stop their bodies getting weaker. So weaken must mean lose strength.
explain: «Komodo dragons have venom glands in their jaws; the venom stops blood clotting and weakens prey.» Prey is the animal being hunted. Test your meaning in the sentence: the venom makes prey less strong, and that still makes sense.
explain: The second meaning is about people. «He weakened and let us stay up late.» He had been saying no, then he gave in. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it fits.
fact: To weaken means to become weaker, or to make something weaker.
fact: «Weakened by illness» means the body has lost strength because of being ill.
fact: Soap «weakens the "skin" of water», which is its surface tension, so a resting paper clip sinks.
fact: The UK children's flu vaccine is a nasal spray with «weakened viruses» that cannot cause flu.
fact: Strengthen is the opposite of weaken: exercise can strengthen muscles.
exercise: «Astronauts' muscles and bones weaken in space, so they exercise.» What does weaken mean here? | Get bigger | Grow brighter | *Become less strong | Move faster
exercise: «He weakened and let us stay up late.» What does weakened mean here? | Got stronger and shouted | Became very angry | *Gave in and changed his mind | Fell asleep early
exercise: Which word is the opposite of weaken? | Weep | Wander | *Strengthen | Weigh
test: «The venom stops blood clotting and weakens prey.» What does the venom do to the prey? | *Makes it less strong | Makes it stronger | Makes it sleepy and calm | Makes it grow larger
test: A drop of washing-up liquid «weakens the skin» of water, so a resting paper clip sinks at once. What does this let happen? | The water freezes | The paper clip floats | *The paper clip sinks | The water dries up
exam: A doctor says, «She is weakened by illness.» What does weakened mean? | Angry with the doctor | Very quiet and calm | *Less strong because she is ill | Feeling strong and fit
